WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.670
- Our next guest had her breakout role

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.400
as Echo in the Disney
Plus series "Hawkeye..."

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.360
I love "Hawkeye."

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.230
A few years ago.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.640
Now she's got her own series.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.560
It's named after her character, Echo,

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.660
and you can also see it on Disney Plus,

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.963
say hello to Alaqua Cox, everybody.

00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:17.963
(audience cheering)

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.820
So everybody, let's welcome Ashley.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.110
This is Alaqua's interpreter.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.643
Welcome Ashley as well.
(audience applauds)

00:00:39.643 --> 00:00:40.530
This is Common.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:41.370
I'm gonna introduce you to Common.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.863
[Ashley] Nice to meet you.

00:00:43.863 --> 00:00:45.600
- Great to meet you, blessings.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.310
- So you're a new mama, right?

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.080
So how's that like?
- Yes.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.570
I'm a new mom to a three month old son.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:52.710
- Oh, you must be are tired.
- He just became three months

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:54.450
old a few days ago.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:55.950
Oh my gosh, he's growing so fast.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.320
I can't believe it, that
time does actually fly.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.330
I truly believe that quote now.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:04.050
- Absolutely. Are you tired? (laughs)

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:06.270
- [Ashley] At first, yes.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:07.110
He probably woke me up four

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:08.370
or five times a night in the beginning.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:09.840
But now he's gotten better with sleeping,

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.610
so I am very fortunate.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.900
I don't wanna jinx it now though.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:13.950
- [Kelly] We're gonna... Here you go.

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.121
That's not wood, there we go.

00:01:15.121 --> 00:01:17.310
(Common laughs)
- Yeah, no, don't jinx it.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.010
So motherhood, what do you
feel like has surprised you?

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.660
Did you always wanna be a mother?

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.770
- [Ashley] I've always wanted to be a mom.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.300
I always wanted many, many kids.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.713
But now with my career,

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.410
I think I might keep it to one or two.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.329
- Yeah, solid move.

00:01:33.329 --> 00:01:34.560
(Common and Kelly laugh)

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.360
That's what I say. (chuckles)

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.550
So how do you go... You
grew up in Wisconsin.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.410
How does one go from
growing up in Wisconsin

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.207
to all of a sudden on "Hawkeye?"

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.290
- [Ashley] My gosh, I
get this question a lot,

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:49.293
but it's just a cool story that I have.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.940
I never had acting on my radar before.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:57.060
A friend of mine sent me the call casting

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.433
for a deaf indigenous
woman in their twenties.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.030
And at first I was apprehensive,

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.640
but then I got the same
text from two other friends

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:08.160
and I thought, "Ooh, there's
no way I'm gonna get it."

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.460
Because her character Maya
does not have an amputated leg.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.560
So I thought there's no
way they would hire me.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.540
And three months later I auditioned,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.700
got the role, and here we are now.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.139
I was so surprised.
(audience applauding)

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:21.810
- It's an amazing story.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:25.680
How do you feel like
this role has an impact

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.510
with the indigenous communities and also,

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.220
anybody wanting to achieve this dream

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.660
that has prosthetics, maybe feel like

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:31.710
they won't get hired for that?

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.253
I mean, you're representing
so many people right now.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.180
- [Ashley] It feels like
a huge honor to be able

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.973
to represent all these
underrepresented communities.

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:46.050
I want kids to be able to see
themselves and feel worthy.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.360
We deserve this space in this moment.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.580
I am so happy Hollywood
is making these changes

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.870
and accommodations for us.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.580
It's a great time to live right now.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.470
- Absolutely, I love that.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:57.540
A positive outlook on it too.
(audience applauding)

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.210
So what you feel like,
Common, you're an actor,

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.860
you do all the things,
you win all the awards.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.080
What do you feel like you've done

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.077
that has had a huge social
impact, obviously "Glory."

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:13.164
- Well, yeah, I mean, I think
being a part of "Glory,"

00:03:13.164 --> 00:03:15.870
the film "Selma," it
really was just bigger

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:19.230
than John and I, or Ava DuVernay.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:22.320
We all collectively put our
hearts and souls into it,

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.210
but it became something that was more

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:27.390
of a movement and it
raised the consciousness.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.840
And I always look at those awards as like,

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:34.680
these are things that allow
me to do more of the work.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.560
So I'm grateful for
them, I'm very grateful.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.350
And I'll receive them, but I
feel like anytime I get one,

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:42.630
I gotta do more for the
people. That's how I feel.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:43.920
- Yeah, well, 'cause you have

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.417
the chance...
(audience applauding)

00:03:45.417 --> 00:03:47.760
Not everybody gets that opportunity.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.490
So explain for everybody
that hasn't seen "Hawkeye,"

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.713
explain Echo and her powers.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.630
- [Ashley] I love Echo.
She's such a cool character.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.010
She's deaf, indigenous, of course.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:00.420
And an amputee, we added that in.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.780
I always love that we can
add that to my identity.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.660
But she's strong, she's
brave, she's fearless.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.760
She's a competitor and her powers,

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.690
they are culturally
related with each other.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.150
So she uses her powers from her ancestors.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.190
It's so crazy to see myself
on the screen behind me.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:20.520
So sorry about that, but
Echo is a very cool person.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.600
- I mean, you look badass.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.181
I'd be like, "That's me."

00:04:23.181 --> 00:04:24.450
"That's me. I did that."

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.333
Well, everybody, here is a
look at Alaqua Cox and Echo.

00:04:30.258 --> 00:04:32.834
(metal and palms thudding)

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:35.497
(intense instrumental music)

00:04:35.497 --> 00:04:36.538
(Echo grunts)

00:04:36.538 --> 00:04:39.054
(foot thuds)
(metal clangs)

00:04:39.054 --> 00:04:41.204
(intense instrumental music)

00:04:41.204 --> 00:04:42.704
(fist and foot thuds)

00:04:42.704 --> 00:04:44.562
(fence clangs)

00:04:44.562 --> 00:04:47.827
(metal clangs)

00:04:47.827 --> 00:04:51.577
(intense instrumental music)

00:04:52.468 --> 00:04:54.451
(audience applauds)

00:04:54.451 --> 00:04:57.233
- That one kick you held up
there, and then said 'no.'

00:04:57.233 --> 00:04:58.440
- That was crazy.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.150
- [Ashley] Yeah, oh my god.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.920
Can you imagine the pain? My leg is metal.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.920
If I hit somebody in the face,
that would be so painful.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.660
But my older brother, when he was 16...

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.700
We are 16 months apart,
I would take off my leg

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.236
and literally hit him with it.

00:05:10.236 --> 00:05:12.694
(Kelly laughs and claps)

00:05:12.694 --> 00:05:13.620
- That's incredible.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:14.730
- That was amazing, what she did.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.530
- That was, oh my gosh.

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:17.610
- [Ashley] Oh gosh, thank you so much.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:18.450
I appreciate that.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.490
- [Kelly] Oh man, if I was ever gonna be

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:21.570
in a Marvel, if I was an actor,

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.718
I'd be like, "Which one is chill?"

00:05:23.718 --> 00:05:24.690
(audience laughing)

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.639
Which one has the power of chill?

00:05:26.639 --> 00:05:28.800
That doesn't have to do all that.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.590
Well, everybody, "Echo"
streams on Disney+.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:32.823
Be sure to check it out.

